    "title": "<p>The WHO Reporting System for Pancreaticobiliary Cytopathology on pancreas FNAB: implied risk of malignancy (ROM) and clinical management options by diagnostic category</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Raza S. Hoda",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 697.9pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"931\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Diagnostic category</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Estimated ROM<sup>a</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Clinical management options<sup>b</sup></span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Insufficient/Inadequate/Non-diagnostic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">5&ndash;25%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Repeat FNAB</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Benign&nbsp;/ Negative for malignancy</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black;\">0&ndash;15%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Correlate clinically</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Atypical</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">30&ndash;40%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Repeat FNAB</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Pancreaticobiliary neoplasm, low-risk/grade (PaN-low)</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black;\">5&ndash;20%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">Correlate clinically</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pancreaticobiliary neoplasm, high-risk/grade (PaN-high)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">60&ndash;95%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Surgical resection in surgically fit patients; conservative management optional</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 23.35pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 23.35pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Suspicious for malignancy</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 23.35pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: black;\">80&ndash;100%</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 23.35pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black;\">If patient to be surgically managed, treat as positive; if patient requires preoperative therapy, repeat FNAB</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 248.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"331\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Malignant</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.45pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\">99&ndash;100%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 329.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"439\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Per clinical stage</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Estimated ROMs are based on retrospective and prospective studies with risk analysis based on pancreatic neoplasia with low-grade and high-grade cytopathological atypia <span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{26618476; 31097287; 31722125; 34623767}</span>. <sup>b</sup>Management options for patients with pancreatic lesions may depend on a variety of factors, including clinical and imaging characteristics and the overall functional status of the patient. Some clinical management suggestions are outlined above.</p>",
